# Spec 0038 — UI standardization: workbench relocation, faceted Materials/Library windows, lifecycle, experiments & inverse wiring

Full spec authored from the operator's preliminary spec
`specs/0038/.manual/006-ui-standardization-preliminary-spec.md` (operator
decisions Q1–Q24 of `003`, Q25–Q29 of `005`, and the three approved
interpretation calls of its §17 are binding). The ordered work lives in
`.spec-jsonl`; this document carries only the binding constraints, the
contract table, and the per-part orientation.

## 0. Binding constraints (every part)

0.1 **Elevate every primitive** (CLAUDE.md). New ids are single-case DUs with a
`.value` accessor plus `create`/`tryCreate`; enumerated conditions are named
multi-case DUs (no naked `bool`, no `enum`); every `*Error` case carries
`reason : string` or a typed payload; public functions have explicit concrete
signatures. Follow the existing elevated-id precedents `MaterialId`
(`…Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:27`) and `SampleId` / the preset DUs
(`…Domain/ElementId.fs:139-192`). The operator's "is-new flag" and "protected
flag" are therefore two-case DUs (`EntryFreshness`, `EntryProtection`), never
bools.

0.2 **No legacy, no fallback, no migration.** No library STATE is persisted:
the Main-flow composition builds every store in memory at startup
(`…App/Program.fs:129-147`, `createInMemory` proxies over the Domain seeds),
so re-typed structures replace old ones cleanly and every app start re-seeds.
The only library-shaped serialization in the tree is metadata-only and
unwired from that composition — the §I.8 share/export file format
(`…Storage/Report.fs:17-24`, module `MaterialLibrary`, whose persisted
`MaterialEntryDto` at `:36` carries display metadata only) and the
import/export helpers (`…Storage/MaterialImport.fs` —
`importRefractiveIndexInfo` `:407`, `importCsv` `:432`, `exportCsv` `:459`);
per §0.3 this spec adds no schema or import/export work, so neither gains a
persisted-state role. The registered write-seam contracts
`STORE_XDUO_0001 MaterialProxy` (`…Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:506`) and
`STORE_XDUO_0002 SampleProxy` (`…Domain/ElementId.fs:318`) keep their names,
kinds, and declaring project; their record surfaces are re-typed **in place**
by IMPLEMENT steps — no temporary, no shim, no compatibility overloads (the
0035 precedent of re-typing `MaterialEntry.category` through the same
surface). The one persisted user file this spec touches, `environment.json`,
is loaded totally with defaults on shape mismatch (`…App/Program.fs:33-35`),
so a re-typed settings field needs **no** migration code: an old file simply
yields the default.

0.3 **No real IO** beyond three named seams. All catalogue, scene, and
experiment IO goes through `[<ReferenceEquality>]` proxy records with
`createInMemory` implementations over private `ref Map`s — the existing seam
(`SampleProxy.createInMemory`, `…Domain/ElementId.fs:652`;
`MaterialProxy.createInMemory`, `:722`). This spec writes NO catalogue, scene,
or experiment files to disk and adds NO schema or import/export work;
`.ocproj` stays unwired. The only real IO permitted: (a) the existing
`environment.json` persistence (`…Ui/UserEnvironment.fs`), (b)
`appsettings.json` through `Softellect.Sys.AppSettings` only, and (c) the thin
measured-data CSV file-read adapter behind `ExperimentDataProxy` (approved
interpretation, preliminary §17.2).

0.4 **UI is testable without a window** (CLAUDE.md). Every new surface is a
pure Domain edit model plus a `State`/`Handlers` record; behaviour is
unit-tested in Domain, structure/interaction in `Avalonia.Headless`
(`ui-smoke`) tests. FuncUI dynamic-list hygiene: generated rows/nodes NEVER
set `StyledElement.Name` — they use `AutomationProperties.AutomationId` (the
documented pattern at `…Controls/MaterialsControls.fs:139-146`) plus per-item
`View.withKey`; filter/text boxes over tree-rebuilding state commit on
Enter/LostFocus, never per keystroke.

0.5 **Interpolated strings, never `sprintf`**; four-space indent; opening `{`
on its own line; a space before every annotation colon; `camelCase` record
fields; LF endings.

0.6 **Zero warnings from our code** (CLAUDE.md); only the third-party NuGet
advisories `NU1701` / `NU1901`–`NU1904` are exempt. The relocation and the new
projects MUST NOT reintroduce `MSB3277` (the WebView2 chain was already
resolved in 0035); anything that appears is fixed at the reference level,
never suppressed.

0.7 **Operator-facing UX checklist** (condensed — this spec introduces new
top-level windows and destructive verbs). *Discoverability:* the product
launcher gains `Main / Inverse / Materials / Library` buttons (this order) and
the constructor's ribbon tab-strip row gains right-aligned `Materials…` /
`Library…` buttons — every window's entry point is named in its step.
*Progress:* every proxy verb is synchronous and in-memory, so there are NO
background jobs and NO progress UI; the one potentially heavy render — tree
materialization above `TreeAutoBuildThreshold` — is gated behind an explicit
Show/Search button (per-tree granularity). *Pre-confirmation:* no LLM calls,
no long-duration work — no gate. *Refresh:* after every verb the owning
window re-queries its proxies in the same MVU render pass — no manual reload
anywhere. *Action buttons:* every opposing pair (Select/Close, Save/Cancel,
Discard/Keep editing) is same-row with a visible gap and distinct
positive/negative styling. *Destructive verbs:* Remove / Supersede / Mark
inactive are confirm-gated inline with typed hard-blocks
(`MaterialStillReferenced`, protected-entry refusals) and NO undo, justified
because the catalogue is in-memory session state a restart re-seeds and used
things cannot be deleted at all. *Committable files:* `appsettings.json` and
the three new project folders collide with nothing in the root `.gitignore`
(checked: only build dirs, `*.binz`, `*.autosave`, and arc-runner logs are
ignored). The spec-writer web pages' hidden-controls treatment does not apply:
these are desktop windows, not web pages.

