## Part A — FuncUI dynamic-list hygiene (CRITICAL — land first)

### A.0 Problem statement

The Selector bay crashes with "Cannot set Name : styled element already
styled": `LibraryControls` sets the write-once `Border.name` on generated,
unkeyed rows (`leafRow`, `…Controls/LibraryControls.fs:112`; `actionButton`,
`:148`), so FuncUI recycling a row across a membership change tries to rename
a styled control. The cure already exists in the same project — the
freely-mutable `AutomationProperties.AutomationId` helper with the explanatory
comment (`…Controls/MaterialsControls.fs:139-146`) and the same precedent
noted in `…Controls/ExperimentControls.fs:261-266`. Latent copies of the
hazard: `…Controls/RotationControls.fs:119`,
`…Controls/RayPositionControls.fs:71`,
`…Controls/ElementPaletteControls.fs:55`, and
`…Controls/ExperimentControls.fs:240,581`. One sweep converts them all and
keys every variable-membership generated list with `View.withKey`. No
behaviour change; immediately shippable.

