## Part E — FacetedTree control and the Materials window

### E.0 Problem statement

`<UICOMP:FacetedTreeControls>` is the domain-free rendering control (pure
`State` + `Handlers`, the `…Controls/MaterialsControls.fs` shape), keyed rows
with AutomationIds only, filter box committing on Enter/LostFocus, breadcrumb
chips, count-previews, representation picker, Show/Search gating, all in a
ScrollViewer. `<UICOMP:MaterialsWindow>` instantiates it over the material
facets as the single-instance Materials window: faceted tree + view panel
(metadata + the embeddable dual-axis chart, `…Controls/EmbeddedChart.fs`) +
the existing verbs Add / Edit / Remove / Categories… rewired to the window.
The Materials bay is REMOVED from the ribbon (`materialsBay` in `mainBays`,
`…TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:2339`); the ribbon tab-strip row
gains the right-aligned `Materials…` button (the constructor-side entry
point; the launcher button lands in Part N).

---

## Part F — Library window; ideal elements become protected entries

### F.0 Problem statement

*Library* = the library of optical elements (samples ∪ polarizers ∪ sources ∪
detectors); *Materials* = homogeneous optical-property descriptions — two
windows, one tree control (operator, Q4). The notion "ideal element"
disappears: the seeded presets (`pol-lp` / `pol-cp-left` / `pol-cp-right` /
`det-intensity` / `det-ellipsometer` / `src-600`,
`…Domain/ElementId.fs:535-540`) become ordinary **protected** library entries
— `EntryProtection = ProtectedBuiltIn | UserManaged`; protected entries
cannot be deleted, marked inactive, or superseded. Seeded SAMPLES remain
`UserManaged` (they are editable examples today — recorded interpretation).
Polarizer behaviour becomes data: `PolarizerBehavior = ComputedIdeal of
PolarizerKind | ConstantMueller of MuellerComponent list` (ordered components
`{ matrix; offset }` stored at reference orientation, rotated
`R(−θ)·M·R(θ)` at run time, product on demand), with
`PolarizerCategory = LpCategory | CpCategory | LpCpCategory | CpLpCategory |
CustomMueller` as the polarizer facet. `ComputedIdeal` synthesizes through
the existing `Propagation.inputStokes` / `analyzerMueller`
(`…Domain/Propagation.fs:54-89`) exactly as today; `ConstantMueller` entries
live ONLY in the Stokes/Mueller pipeline (never the Berreman stack). The
dedicated editor for `ConstantMueller` entries is explicitly OUT OF SCOPE
(operator, 001) — the DU makes it a non-breaking future addition.
`<UICOMP:LibraryWindow>` is the single-instance Library window over the whole
`LibraryEntry` corpus (`…Domain/ElementId.fs:188-192`, via `LibraryProxy`
`:276-281` + `SampleProxy` for the sample verbs), default representation "By
kind"; the Library bay (`samplesBay`,
`…TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:2340`) is removed the same way
as Materials.

