## Part J — Table visuals: bound / unbound / out-of-band

### J.0 Problem statement

The renderer input `Drawable` (`…TestWindows/ElementRenderer.fs:26-32`) gains
a three-valued `BindingState` (bound / unbound / not-bindable — lens and
mirrors are not bindable and render normally): unbound draws a dashed outline
with ghosted fill (pattern, not hue — colorblind-safe); bound stays solid;
the readout/Details keep the text. Independently, an **out-of-band**
indicator (operator, Q22/Q29): an element flags when it is bound, some
material reachable through its binding is dispersive, and the wavelengths
**the actual experiment requests** (a single λ for a fixed setting; the full
range for a sweep — 600 nm inside a 300–700 nm band is fine, a 200–800 nm
sweep is not) fall partly outside the union of that material's defined
dispersion segments (`EditSegment.interval`,
`…Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:100-102`). Visual: a small warning badge
plus a hover tooltip naming the offending material(s) with defined vs
requested ranges; the same text in the Details bay. Constant materials never
flag.

