## Part K — Editor rework

### K.0 Problem statement

The Material editor's `DockPanel` layout squeezes the ladder and the preview
into one column (`…TestWindows/MaterialEditorView.fs:1067-1132`); it becomes
two panes split by a vertical splitter — the progressive ladder left inside a
ScrollViewer, the chart right at full height. The single-curve preview
(`n = Re[√ε₁₁]` / `k = Im[√ε₁₁]` only — `…TestWindows/NkDispersionChart.fs:40-64`)
becomes **tabbed multi-curve charts**: tab *n, k* — all principal axes
(n_x/n_y/n_z left, k_x/k_y/k_z right) with legend and per-series toggles; tab
*Gyration* — g components vs λ, present only when optically active (series
assembled through the engine's `RhoWithDispValue.toRhoWithDisp`,
`OpticalProperties/Active.fs:152`); tab *μ* — Polder components vs λ, only
when magnetic (`MuWithDispValue.toMuWithDisp`,
`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:671`). Tabs appear/disappear with the ladder
toggles. Both editors gain unsaved-edit confirmation: dirty = structural
inequality between the load-captured edit state and the current one (no
flags), intercepting BOTH Cancel and window close — today `CancelClicked`
closes silently (`…TestWindows/MaterialEditorView.fs:423-424`,
`…TestWindows/SampleEditorView.fs:549-550`).

---

## Part L — Inverse problem: wiring only (the solver is out of scope)

### L.0 Problem statement

This part wires the inverse-problem FLOW; no solving, no normalization — data
is gathered raw and corrections belong to the future solver (operator, Q23).
The launcher's `Inverse` opens the same constructor in an inverse state: the
sample element unbound (dashed, Part J) or bound to a HINT sample; no hint ⇒
no experiment chart; hint ⇒ chart as today. The user builds an experiment
collection (Part I experiments, each possibly sample-less/dark) and attaches
**one data file per experiment**. Strict v1 schemas: intensity — first row
labels (ignored), then comma-separated `X,Y`, invariant culture, typed parse
errors, the X column meaning whatever the experiment's varied parameter says,
and a range/units mismatch against the experiment a LOUD typed validation
error; ellipsometric — `wavelength_nm, psi_deg, delta_deg` (+ optional
`aoi_deg`), one file per experiment; NCS / Mueller-element imports are future
parsers, not schema changes. Parsers are PURE (`string -> Result<…>`, the
text-taking precedent `SpectralImport.parseSpectrumCsv`,
`…Storage/SpectralImport.fs`), tested against in-memory strings; file access
sits behind `<STORE:ExperimentDataProxy>` with a mock for every test and a
thin real-file adapter as the runtime wiring (§0.3c). The file picker starts
at the persisted last folder and updates it only on a confirmed selection —
wiring the inert `EnvironmentSettings.lastFolders`
(`…Ui/UserEnvironment.fs:184`, persisted but never read by any picker),
re-typed to a purpose-keyed map per §0.2. The flow ends at
`<UICOMP:SolverHandoffWindow>`: a summary of the received collection
(experiments, setups, detector kinds, attached files, per-file
parse/validation status) plus the message that the actual solver will be done
separately; it performs basic validation (all elements except sample
specified; every experiment has a readable, schema-valid file; ranges
consistent) and reports typed errors.

---

## Part M — Storage scaffolding

### M.0 Problem statement

Two proofs, no product coupling (operator, Q24 + 001). (1) A nearly-empty C#
EFC project `OpticalConstructor.Database` — one `Test` table, a
`TestDbContext`, an initial migration; provider (MSSQL/SQLite) and connection
strings from `appsettings.json` via `AppSettingsProvider.tryGetConnectionString`;
modeled on the STL example (`C:/GitHub/Softellect/Apps/DistrProc/Migrations/Common/CommonDbContext.cs`).
Its only purpose is proving EFC wiring creates/migrates — **the app does not
reference or use it**, and the proof runs against SQLite in a test (no MSSQL
server required). (2) An F# seeding project `OpticalConstructor.Seeding`
taking a `<STORE:SeedingProxy>` (a record of `Result`-returning `save…`
functions) and pushing the EXISTING Domain seed values — `standardCategories`
(`…Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:118`), `builtInEntries` (`:363`),
`SeedSamples` (`…Domain/ElementId.fs:381`), `seedEntries` (`:532`) — which
stay where they live, close to the source. Today's implementation of the
proxy is the in-memory stores, i.e. seeding runs with no database at all;
seeded Guids are frozen forever (future foreign keys).

---

## Part N — Consolidations, launcher, warnings, composition

### N.0 Problem statement

Two parallel recent-file stores exist — `EnvironmentSettings.recentFiles`
(`…Ui/UserEnvironment.fs:185`) and the bounded-MRU module
`…Storage/RecentFiles.fs` — ONE remains (the Storage module, keeping its pure
`bump` invariant; the environment field is removed). Automation ids
consolidate into ONE `[<Literal>]` constants module replacing the per-control
`UiIds` modules (id VALUES unchanged, so tests only re-point). The product
launcher becomes `Main / Inverse / Materials / Library` (this order) with
stable names and automation ids. A final warning sweep holds §0.6, and the
closing WIRE_UI step composes everything at the root and drives the whole
surface headless.

